1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:02,360
Matthew, 25

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:09,120
Then the kingdom of heaven will be like ten virgins who took their lamps and went to meet

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:09,820
the bridegroom.

4
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:16,160
Five of them were foolish, and five were wise, for when the foolish took their lamps, they

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:20,900
took no oil with them, but the wise took flasks of oil with their lamps.

6
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:25,680
As the bridegroom was delayed, they all became drowsy and slept.

7
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:30,020
But at midnight there was a cry, Here is the bridegroom!

8
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,580
Come out to meet him!

9
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:34,700
Then all those virgins rose and trimmed their lamps.

10
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:40,900
And the foolish said to the wise, Give us some of your oil, for our lamps are going

11
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:41,280
out.

12
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:47,000
But the wise answered, saying, Since there will not be enough for us and for you, go

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,300
rather to the dealers and buy for yourselves.

14
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:55,380
And while they were going to buy, the bridegroom came, and those who were ready went in with

15
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:55,580
him.

16
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,340
To the marriage feast, and the door was shut.

17
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:04,680
Afterward the other virgins came also, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.

18
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:10,220
But he answered, Truly I say to you, I do not know you.

19
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:15,420
Watch therefore, for you know neither the day nor the hour.

20
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:22,420
For it will be like a man going on a journey, who called his servants and entrusted to them

21
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,100
his property.

22
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:25,580
To one he gave five talents.

23
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,300
To another two, to another one.

24
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,680
To each according to his ability.

25
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:32,800
Then he went away.

26
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:38,660
He who had received the five talents went at once and traded with them, and he made

27
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:39,980
five talents more.

28
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:44,720
So also he who had the two talents made two talents more.

29
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:50,800
But he who had received the one talent went and dug in the ground and hid his master's

30
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:51,060
money.

31
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,660
Now after a long time, the master of those five talents, who had received the one talent,

32
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,500
came and settled accounts with them.

33
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:04,260
And he who had received the five talents came forward bringing five talents more, saying,

34
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:07,460
Master, you delivered to me five talents.

35
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,280
Here, I have made five talents more.

36
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:16,420
His master said to him, Well done, good and faithful servant.

37
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,940
You have been faithful over a little.

38
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,260
I will set you over much.

39
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,420
Enter into the joy of your master.

40
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:24,580
Enter into the joy of your master.

41
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:31,100
And he also who had the two talents came forward, saying, Master, you delivered to

42
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:31,960
me two talents.

43
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,240
Here, I have made two talents more.

44
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:40,280
His master said to him, Well done, good and faithful servant.

45
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:43,040
You have been faithful over a little.

46
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,360
I will set you over much.

47
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,340
Enter into the joy of your master.

48
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:55,660
He also who had received the one talent came forward, saying, Master, I have made five

49
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,000
talents.

50
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,160
Here, I have made five talents more.

51
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,260
Your master answer him, Through Amazing Word you have materialized many things, and I are

52
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:02,840
now better than they thought they were, but not as strong as you thought they were.

53
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,340
So I knew you to be a hard man, reaping where you did not sow, and gathering where you scattered

54
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:05,340
no seed.

55
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:07,220
So I was afraid, and I went and hid your talent in the ground.

56
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:10,680
Here, you have what is yours.

57
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:15,260
But his master answered him, You wicked and slothful servant, you knew that I reap where

58
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:20,620
I have not sown, and gather where I scattered no seed.

59
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,400
Then you ought to have invested my money with the bankers.

60
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,600
You ought to have invested my money with the bankers.

61
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:24,820
You ought to have invested my money with the bankers.

62
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,520
You ought to have invested my money with the bankers.

63
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,580
and at my coming I should have received what was my own with interest.

64
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:34,540
So take the talent from him, and give it to him who has the ten talents.

65
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:39,420
For to everyone who has will more be given, and he will have an abundance.

66
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:43,960
But from the one who has not, even what he has will be taken away.

67
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,300
And cast the worthless servant into the outer darkness.

68
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:51,580
In that place there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.

69
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:57,740
When the Son of Man comes in his glory, and all the angels with him,

70
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,580
then he will sit on his glorious throne.

71
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:06,580
Before him will be gathered all the nations, and he will separate people one from another,

72
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:09,900
as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats.

73
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:14,660
And he will place the sheep on his right, but the goats on the left.

74
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:18,060
Then the king will say to those on his right,

75
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:21,260
Come, you who are blessed by my Father.

76
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:25,800
Inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.

77
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:29,220
For I was hungry, and you gave me food.

78
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,820
I was thirsty, and you gave me drink.

79
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,460
I was a stranger, and you welcomed me.

80
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:37,120
I was naked, and you clothed me.

81
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,380
I was sick, and you visited me.

82
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,400
I was in prison, and you came to me.

83
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:45,720
Then the righteous will answer him, saying,

84
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:51,220
Lord, when did we see you hungry and feed you, or thirsty and give you drink?

85
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:57,080
And when did we see you a stranger and welcome you, or naked and clothe you?

86
00:04:57,680 --> 00:05:01,240
And when did we see you sick or in prison and visit you?

87
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,400
And the king will answer them,

88
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:08,740
Truly I say to you, as you did it to one of the least of these my brothers,

89
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,460
you did it to me.

90
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:13,540
Then he will say to those on his left,

91
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:20,000
Depart from me, you cursed, into the eternal fire prepared for the devil and his angels.

92
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:21,560
For I was hungry, and you gave me food.

93
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:24,100
I was hungry, and you gave me no food.

94
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,840
I was thirsty, and you gave me no drink.

95
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:30,220
I was a stranger, and you did not welcome me.

96
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:32,540
Naked, and you did not clothe me.

97
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:36,440
Sick, and in prison, and you did not visit me.

98
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:39,820
Then they also will answer, saying,

99
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:47,020
Lord, when did we see you hungry, or thirsty, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison,

100
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,180
and did not minister to you?

101
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,540
Then he will answer them, saying,

102
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:57,280
Truly I say to you, as you did not do it to one of the least of these,

103
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,520
you did not do it to me.

104
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:03,260
And these will go away into eternal punishment,

105
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:06,700
but the righteous into eternal life.

